## Learnings from previous web searches

- vterm is a full terminal emulator designed for interactive use, not just command execution
- <cite>vterm inserts fake-newlines purely for rendering</cite> which need to be filtered out
- Process termination in vterm works differently than regular subprocesses - need to use process sentinels
- vterm provides excellent performance and full ANSI/color support but requires careful management
- The key is to properly handle the vterm lifecycle and process termination detection

